WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.602
-Thanks for remembering!

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.037
-That's exactly -- Welcome.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:06.672
-I'm still hurting
over that Password loss.

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:09.308
-[ Laughing ]
Oh, my gosh. I got to say,

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:10.543
thank you so much

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.745
for coming back to my show.
I appreciate it.

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:15.214
-Well, let me just say something
to you, truthfully,

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:18.618
and just before you jump into
all your prepared notes,

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:21.220
I was going to say that, really,

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.490
of all the NBC late night shows
currently on the air,

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.725
this is in my top two.

00:00:26.725 --> 00:00:28.127
-Thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:30.396
-Yeah. And, you know, I would
do the show way more often

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:32.532
but, you know...pride.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:34.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.370
-Hey.
-No, seriously, seriously,

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.539
I just -- Seriously,
I just want to say

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:41.240
that you have been here
every night

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.809
during this incredible crisis.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:45.778
You've been doing great work,
hilariously funny,

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:48.815
and it's very comforting
to have you, so thank you.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.116
-Wow.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.252
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.753 --> 00:00:55.788
Thank you.

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:57.891
-Okay, now do me.

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:00.359
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:01.461
-This the way it works?

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:04.964
Steve Martin,
I think you are a genius.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.632
-Oh, I wasn't expecting that.

00:01:06.632 --> 00:01:07.901
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.535
-Thank you. Wow.

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:12.238
-Hey, when did you remove
your Robert E. Lee statue?

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:15.174
Backstage, it was
such a tradition to see that.

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:17.076
-Yeah, yeah, and I moved it.
[ Laughs ]

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:18.911
Yeah, it must have
thrown you off backstage.

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:20.746
But, well,
I've got to be honest,

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:21.815
you guys both look fantastic.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:23.215
-Oh, come on.
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:01:23.215 --> 00:01:25.251
The pandemic is a challenge.
But I'll tell you one thing.

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:28.253
It was great to go around
the house for a year and a half

00:01:28.253 --> 00:01:29.522
wearing no bra.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.157
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.960
And I let my hair go gray,
and I'm going to keep it.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.295
-Oh, wow.

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:37.062
-You look fantastic, by the way.

00:01:37.062 --> 00:01:38.264
You never -- You really --

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:41.034
Is it the horse deworming
medication you're taking?

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:43.069
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:45.605
-I want to talk about
"Only Murders in the Building."

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:49.675
This is the most-watched comedy
premiere in the history of Hulu.

00:01:49.675 --> 00:01:52.078
It's a major hit.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.412
It's a major hit.

00:01:53.412 --> 00:01:55.081
You're great in it.

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:57.050
I'll tell you who's fantastic,
Selena Gomez.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.985
-Unbelievable.
-Selena Gomez is fantastic.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:02.488
-Hello. I'm also in it.

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:03.890
Steve's in it -- Let's go back.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.758
Steve's great. Selena's great.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.427
-Yeah, no -- Yeah.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:08.728
-She is fantastic.

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:11.064
She came in our trailer
for the first time,

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:13.733
and she said, "Gee,
it smells like Grandma's house."

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:15.602
-Aww, that's sweet, you know?

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.737
-Yeah.
-No, she's an amazing actress.

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.238
And this is how I know
she's a great actress --

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:22.241
'cause when she met us,
she acted like she knew us.

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:23.676
-Aww.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.411
-The nice thing about Selena...
-What?

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.447
-She lays out our pills
for us in the morning.

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:30.516
-I mean, this is why
I can feel the chemistry.

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:32.885
Now, I'm about to show
everyone a clip.

00:02:32.885 --> 00:02:34.954
Can you tell us what we're about
to see here?

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:38.858
-Yeah, well, we chose this clip
because you're in it.

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:41.227
You did us a favor.
Tina Fey is in it.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:43.496
Nathan Lane is in it.
Marty and I are in it.

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.697
-Sting is in it.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.332
-Well -- What?
-Sting.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:47.366
-He's mentioned.

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:48.634
-Yes.
-He's not in the clip.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.569
-Oh, no, sorry.
-Yeah, yeah, that's okay.

00:02:50.569 --> 00:02:52.572
I think I can do this.
I can handle it.

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:55.875
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.043
♪♪

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:58.844
I think --
-Yeah.

00:02:58.844 --> 00:03:01.180
-Anybody else you want
to be in the clip?

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:02.715
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:03.983
-Hey, Springsteen's in it!

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:06.419
-Beyoncé's in it.
-Oh, she's so good.

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:07.753
-Marlon Brando, and he's dead.

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:09.321
-Marlon Brando's in it.
He's dead, and he's still in it.

00:03:09.321 --> 00:03:10.423
Okay, I'm sorry.
I'm going to stop now.

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:11.757
-Maybe we should just
show the clip.

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:13.559
-Or, yeah.
-Let it speak for itself.

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:16.195
-Yep. Well, it's your show.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:18.097
Let's take a look at
"Only Murders in the Building."

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:19.131
Take a look.

00:03:19.131 --> 00:03:21.434
-The title of their podcast is

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:25.104
"Dimas Chicken Wraps Presents:

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.773
Only Murders in the Building."

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:29.175
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:35.715
-Well, I do love
Dimas Chicken Wraps.

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:37.149
[ TV shuts off ]

00:03:37.149 --> 00:03:40.653
-Teddy, do you understand

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:43.021
how huge Fallon is in Greece?

00:03:43.021 --> 00:03:44.490
[ Audience laughing ]

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.526
Do you know what my cousins
back on Nisyros are going to do

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:50.396
when they see this?

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:53.065
They're going to [bleep]
themselves, Oli!

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:56.101
They're going to squat
right down on their goat fields

00:03:56.101 --> 00:03:59.171
and [bleep] themselves in envy!

00:03:59.171 --> 00:04:01.040
[ Laughs ]

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.076
-[ Chuckles ]

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:05.311
-That's fantastic!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:08.214
-There's no one funnier
and no one more perfect

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:09.915
in everything he does
than Nathan Lane.

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:12.018
-Nathan Lane was spectacular --
And you were, too.

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:14.854
But Nathan Lane
is a professional and --

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:16.789
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:18.691
-What does that mean?
-Oh, it --

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:21.561
-It was a stretch for Jimmy.
He was playing a talk show host.

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:24.497
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:26.532
-I want to congratulate you
again on this.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.267
It's a big, giant hit on Hulu.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:30.236
Check it out.
"Only Murders in the Building."

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:32.338
Before you guys go,
I would just like to --

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:33.673
-Oh, we're going?

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:34.974
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:36.943
-You don't have to.
-I get that a lot at parties.

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:38.044
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:39.612
-"Hey, before you go."
-"Before you go."

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:41.680
-You go, "I just got here."
Yeah.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.849
I wanted to see
if you wanted to say something

00:04:43.849 --> 00:04:46.319
about our friend Norm Macdonald
who passed away.

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:47.587
-Oh, my God.
-Funny.

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:49.555
-Yeah.
-There was no one funnier.

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:51.123
Brilliant Canadian.

00:04:51.123 --> 00:04:53.126
-You know, we do --

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:54.960
In our show,
we do a tribute to comedians.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.430
I'm serious about this.
And we name different comedians,

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.298
like Bob Newhart and people.

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:02.268
And we do a tribute
to Norm Macdonald,

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:04.170
and we use one of his lines.
We say --

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:07.339
And this is one of his lines --
He said,

00:05:07.339 --> 00:05:10.410
"There's only two categories
of cliff diving --

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:13.346
grand champion
and stuff on a rock."

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:15.881
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:19.485
-But I really think
that in comedy, particularly,

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:21.587
the originals
stand out the most,

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:23.689
and they stay with us
long after they're gone.

00:05:23.689 --> 00:05:26.758
And there was no one more
original than Norm Macdonald.

00:05:26.758 --> 00:05:29.762
There was no one
who did his style.

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:31.531
There was no one who
had his rhythms.

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:34.433
He was remarkable
and so kind and funny.

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:36.068
-Yeah, I just figured
I'd get your thoughts.

00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:37.570
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:40.739
You guys are the greatest.
Steve Martin, Martin Short.

00:05:40.739 --> 00:05:42.408
"Only Murders in the Building"
on Hulu.

